WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.637
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Friday, November twentieth.

2
00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:12.447
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.447 --> 00:00:15.063
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:30.125
Today: Australia lowers its advice for Oman and Jordan, Iraqi forces move into a Kataib Hezbollah stronghold, a Houthi strike hits Riyadh's tallest tower, a deadly attack on Kyiv, and new U.S. sanctions on Southeast Asian scam networks.

5
00:00:30.125 --> 00:00:30.945
First, travel advice.

6
00:00:30.945 --> 00:00:43.478
Smartraveller, Australia's travel advisory service, has lowered its overall level for Oman to exercise a high degree of caution, citing the unpredictable security situation in the region.

7
00:00:43.478 --> 00:00:48.708
It still advises reconsidering travel to areas within thirty kilometers of the Yemen border.

8
00:00:48.708 --> 00:01:01.166
Smartraveller also lowered Jordan to exercise a high degree of caution, citing the regional situation and the threat of terrorism, and still advises reconsidering travel to the Syrian and Iraqi border regions.

9
00:01:01.166 --> 00:01:02.573
Turning to Iraq.

10
00:01:02.573 --> 00:01:11.223
Reuters reports Iraqi security forces began deploying in Jurf al Sakhr, a stronghold of the Kataib Hezbollah armed group south of Baghdad, under a compromise deal.

11
00:01:11.223 --> 00:01:18.074
Al Arabiya reports the spokesperson for the commander in chief of Iraq's armed forces said the redeployment is proceeding normally.

12
00:01:18.074 --> 00:01:25.085
Al Jazeera reports the government had given the group until today to withdraw.

13
00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:25.960
Next, an update on the Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia.

14
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:34.453
Reuters reports Riyadh's tallest skyscraper, the headquarters of the Saudi sovereign wealth fund, was struck in a Houthi attack.

15
00:01:34.453 --> 00:01:50.536
Separately, the State Department issued an alert for Kuwait telling Americans in the Middle East to exercise heightened vigilance, citing the threat of attacks by Iranian supported Houthis and Iranian efforts to target U.S. government officials and facilities.

16
00:01:50.536 --> 00:02:02.787
In Ukraine, Radio Free Europe Radio Liberty reports Russia launched a combined drone and ballistic missile attack on Kyiv, killing at least three people and injuring fifteen, according to local officials.

17
00:02:02.787 --> 00:02:11.971
And on sanctions, the Treasury Department's Office of Foreign Assets Control sanctioned cyber scam operators and armed group facilitators in Southeast Asia.

18
00:02:11.971 --> 00:02:16.743
The State Department says the scam centers are run mostly by Chinese organized crime and fuel human trafficking.

19
00:02:16.743 --> 00:02:25.779
Treasury also sanctioned two drug trafficking organizations, the Australia based Comanchero Outlaw Motorcycle Gang and Italy's 'Ndrangheta.

20
00:02:25.779 --> 00:02:29.891
Now a few quick notes by region.

21
00:02:29.891 --> 00:02:32.934
In the Middle East, an update on the Strait of Hormuz.

22
00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:39.724
Al Arabiya and Iran International report Iran's Revolutionary Guard says two supertankers hit naval mines and exploded in the strait.

23
00:02:39.724 --> 00:02:51.566
And the Institute for the Study of War assesses the Houthis may be conducting an offensive in Yemen's Abyan province to tie down government aligned forces that could reinforce Aden.

24
00:02:51.566 --> 00:02:52.741
In Africa, the U.S.

25
00:02:52.741 --> 00:03:02.348
Embassy in Ethiopia says violence continues in remote parts of Tigray near the border with Eritrea and the security situation may change at any time.

26
00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:12.027
In Sudan, the U.N. humanitarian office says air strikes reportedly hit a village in the Kordofan region, killing fifteen civilians, including four children.

27
00:03:12.027 --> 00:03:18.296
In Asia, Reuters reports Cyclone Akvan made landfall on India's eastern coast with heavy rain, the third such storm to hit the country in less than a month.

28
00:03:18.296 --> 00:03:28.233
And BBC Africa reports the International Court of Justice ruled that Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya, in a case brought by The Gambia.

29
00:03:28.233 --> 00:03:37.091
In Europe, Travel Canada says all border crossings between Russia and Estonia will close starting December first.

30
00:03:37.091 --> 00:03:48.687
In cyber news, The Record reports Ukrainian authorities arrested four suspected members of an international ransomware network accused of extorting more than forty million dollars from companies worldwide.

31
00:03:48.687 --> 00:04:00.302
In the Americas, on Wednesday, November eighteenth, Salvadoran President Nayib Bukele announced that Salvadoran troops destroyed the house of a gang leader in Haiti, RFI and DW report.

32
00:04:00.302 --> 00:04:01.807
That's today's brief.

33
00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:10.099
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

34
00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:18.544
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

35
00:04:18.544 --> 00:04:20.810
This brief is digitally narrated.

36
00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:21.806
Questions?

37
00:04:21.806 --> 00:04:25.314
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

38
00:04:25.314 --> 00:04:27.601
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
